<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What a host is told about this widget before it ever draws one.

  updatePeriodMillis is zero, which switches the widget framework's own periodic update off. Its
  floor is thirty minutes and it wakes a sleeping device in order to run; on a television that
  means waking up to fetch data nobody is looking at. WIDGORA pushes its own updates instead.

  One declared size, deliberately. The cell grid belongs to the host, and the host this is aimed
  at does not exist yet, so a second declared size would be a guess dressed up as a choice. The
  dp figures are what decides on a host without a grid, and the cell figures are what decides on
  one with a grid from Android 12 onwards; both are given because a host that ignores one reads
  the other.

  The smallest size a resize may reach is now the declared size itself, and that is a correction
  rather than a preference. It used to be 240 × 120 dp, which this widget cannot draw: on a
  television at that height the bottom line was cut in half and the line below it was missing
  altogether. Declaring a size is a promise to every host that reads it, and the promise now
  matches what the smallest layout actually needs. The figures live in WidgetSizes as well, and
  a test holds the two against each other.

  There is no android:configure yet. Choosing which instance a widget shows, and whether it may
  name individual monitors, is a later step; until then a widget shows the first instance and
  never a name.

  previewLayout is read from Android 12 onwards and renders this widget's own layout at its
  default size, which is why that layout's default texts say that nothing has loaded rather than
  showing a specimen value. Below Android 12 a host falls back to previewImage, and there is none,
  so such a host shows the application icon in its picker.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/widget_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_counts_compact"
    android:maxResizeHeight="320dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="640dp"
    android:minHeight="170dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="170dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="300dp"
    android:minWidth="300dp"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_counts_compact"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
